# The documented read-only set (docs/common.md "Running on a Read-Only
# Filesystem", Docker example): root filesystem read-only, runtime directories
# as tmpfs, and the work directory as the one writable mount (anonymous tmpfs
# starts empty — the documented tmpfs/emptyDir case the boot must seed).
--read-only
--tmpfs /run
--tmpfs /tmp
--tmpfs /var/lib/nginx
--tmpfs /var/log/nginx
--tmpfs /container/work
